BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w7-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy ride 60-75 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy ride 60-75 min - the day after the long day. Ze
 ro impact. THIS IS THE FIRST THING TO CUT when work bites.\n\nWeek 7 of 
 17 - Build\nRESET WEEK. Two corrections that change everything. (1) You 
 have steep terrain 20-25 MINUTES away - Zuid-Kennemerland dunes by train
 \, faces at 30-45%. I told you the nearest hills were 2.5-3 h\; that was
  wrong. (2) Your plan's vertical is an ORDER OF MAGNITUDE short: 40 min/
 week is ~400 m against a 2\,003 m race. From here everything is measured
  in time and vertical metres\, never kilometres. LOCKED WEEK SHAPE: Sun 
 optional easy ride - MON REST - TUE legs + preconditioning walk ONLY (th
 is is THE eccentric day - keep it focused\, no upper) - WED easy run + s
 trides + push - THU vertical + pull - FRI REST - SAT LONG DAY. Eccentric
  work sits 48 h apart throughout: Tue heavy\, Thu moderate\, Sat long. T
 hat spacing is the constraint - force loss needs 3 days to recover and s
 oreness 4\, so 24 h between eccentric sessions compounds damage instead 
 of building tolerance. Cutbacks weeks 10 and 13. CUT ORDER: (1) Sunday r
 ide\, (2) Thursday vertical. Never Saturday's long day or Tuesday's legs
 . HYROX SEEDING STARTS: only via substitution inside Thursday's pull ses
 sion - erg warm-up\, farmers carry\, dead hangs. NOT wall balls\, sandba
 g lunges or burpee broad jumps - those are all quad and eccentric load c
 ompeting directly with the descent block. NOT compromised running - it b
 reaks the 80/20 distribution Madeira needs. The point is to arrive in No
 vember with technique and grip already built\, so the first two Hyrox we
 eks are productive instead of remedial.\n77 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w7-s1-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260819
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260820
SUMMARY:Easy run 6 km
DESCRIPTION:Easy run 6 km (talk test) + 6-8 x 20 s strides after (relaxed
 \, full recovery\, not a workout)\n\nWeek 7 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR under
  158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nRESET WEEK. Two corrections that chan
 ge everything. (1) You have steep terrain 20-25 MINUTES away - Zuid-Kenn
 emerland dunes by train\, faces at 30-45%. I told you the nearest hills 
 were 2.5-3 h\; that was wrong. (2) Your plan's vertical is an ORDER OF M
 AGNITUDE short: 40 min/week is ~400 m against a 2\,003 m race. From here
  everything is measured in time and vertical metres\, never kilometres. 
