 g three different jobs: HEAVY BILATERAL trap-bar deadlift 4 x 4-6 at 80-
 85% 1RM (~72-78 kg)\, LOADED UNILATERAL Bulgarian split squat 3 x 8/leg 
 with dumbbells\, and TEMPO ECCENTRIC step-downs 3 x 8-10/leg with 3-4 s 
 lowering. Then Nordics 3 x 5 and single-leg calf raises. Never to failur
 e. 48-72 h before the long day. On a -15% descent hip drop is 23.7 mm vs
  7.6 mm uphill (very large effect)\, so descending is a frontal-plane hi
 p problem and not only a quad problem - loaded Bulgarians carry that dem
 and\, which is why standalone side planks and cable abduction came out. 
 HYROX SLED TECHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% load (~100 kg)
 \, 60-90 s rest. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms hooked on t
 he posts\, 30-45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3-4 per secon
 d\, and never let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENTRIC\, so it 
 costs your descent block nothing - which is why it is the one Hyrox stat
 ion you can train now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of horizontal 
 force to break a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one rolling\, so l
 earning not to stop is worth more to you than to anyone heavier. About 8
  minutes.\n\nWeek 9 of 17 - Build\nGUT TRAINING STARTS. Target 60-80 g c
 arb/h by week 14\, from 40-50 now\, +10 g every two weeks. No drop bags 
 and no crew at Madeira - only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart - so you car
 ry 400-500 g of carbohydrate yourself. Rehearse the weight and the stowa
 ge\, not just the products. INTENSITY STARTS THIS WEEK. Thursday's verti
 cal becomes intervals - the plan had no hard sessions at all through wee
 ks 7-8\, which was a gap. Target distribution is 80-85% easy\, 15-20% ha
 rd\, with the hard work on incline.\n61 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w9-s4-vertical@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260904
SUMMARY:▲ VERTICAL 60 min WITH INTERVALS
DESCRIPTION:VERTICAL 60 min WITH INTERVALS - stairwell. Warm up 10 min st
 eady\, then 3 x (5 min HARD up at 90-95% HRmax + 3 min EASY SkiErg or ro
 wer). Walk down between reps. Steady climbing for whatever time is left.
  This is the only hard session of your week and it does two jobs: uphill
  intervals for Madeira (the research wants 15-20% of training hard\, nea
 rly all of it on incline) and compromised running for Hyrox. The erg sta
 tions are deliberate - upper-body and aerobic\, so they add nothing to t
 he eccentric load your quads are already carrying.\n\nWeek 9 of 17 - Bui
 ld\nGUT TRAINING STARTS. Target 60-80 g carb/h by week 14\, from 40-50 n
 ow\, +10 g every two weeks. No drop bags and no crew at Madeira - only ~
 2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart - so you carry 400-500 g of carbohydrate yo
 urself. Rehearse the weight and the stowage\, not just the products. INT
 ENSITY STARTS THIS WEEK. Thursday's vertical becomes intervals - the pla
 n had no hard sessions at all through weeks 7-8\, which was a gap. Targe
 t distribution is 80-85% easy\, 15-20% hard\, with the hard work on incl
 ine.\n59 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w9-s5-pull@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260904
SUMMARY:Pull (upper)
DESCRIPTION:Pull (upper) - after the vertical session. HYROX SEEDING\, al
 l substitutions not additions: (1) WARM UP ON THE SKIERG OR ROWER\, 5-8 
 min\, technique only - hinge and drive the first third of the pull\, tha
 t is where 80% of ski power comes from. Replaces your normal warm-up\, c
 osts nothing. (2) SWAP one row variation for a HEAVY FARMERS CARRY\, 4 x
  40-60 m. Same pulling pattern\, direct Hyrox transfer. (3) Finish with 
 DEAD HANGS\, 2-3 x max\, target 90 s by October. Grip takes 4-6 weeks to
  change and it is what limits the farmers carry. About 3 minutes total a
 dded to the session.\n\nWeek 9 of 17 - Build\nGUT TRAINING STARTS. Targe
 t 60-80 g carb/h by week 14\, from 40-50 now\, +10 g every two weeks. No
  drop bags and no crew at Madeira - only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart -
  so you carry 400-500 g of carbohydrate yourself. Rehearse the weight an
 d the stowage\, not just the products. INTENSITY STARTS THIS WEEK. Thurs
 day's vertical becomes intervals - the plan had no hard sessions at all 
 through weeks 7-8\, which was a gap. Target distribution is 80-85% easy\
 , 15-20% hard\, with the hard work on incline.\n59 days to Ultra X Madei
 ra 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
