UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w9-s8-descent@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:▼ PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK
DESCRIPTION:PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK - 5 minutes\, 5.6 kg in the pac
 k\, walking DOWN stairs. Lift up\, walk down\, repeat for 5 min. ~110 m 
 of descent\, about 37 flights. One bout cuts strength loss 49%\, CK 47%\
 , soreness 66% a week later. Five minutes\, in your own building\, no tr
 avel.\n\nWeek 9 of 17 - Build\nGUT TRAINING STARTS. Target 60-80 g carb/
 h by week 14\, from 40-50 now\, +10 g every two weeks. No drop bags and 
 no crew at Madeira - only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart - so you carry 4
 00-500 g of carbohydrate yourself. Rehearse the weight and the stowage\,
  not just the products. INTENSITY STARTS THIS WEEK. Thursday's vertical 
 becomes intervals - the plan had no hard sessions at all through weeks 7
 -8\, which was a gap. Target distribution is 80-85% easy\, 15-20% hard\,
  with the hard work on incline.\n61 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
