SUMMARY:THRESHOLD (8 km)
DESCRIPTION:THRESHOLD - 4 x 5 min comfortably hard\, 90 s easy jog betwee
 n. Warm up 10 min\, cool down 10 min. Effort: you can say three or four 
 words\, not a sentence. HR roughly 160-168. Pace off the week 10 TT. Thr
 eshold first\, not VO2max - it recovers faster and it is what raises the
  pace you can hold.\n\nWeek 11 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR under 158. Walk th
 e climbs. Talk test.\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #1 of 2 - Posbank/Veluwezoom\, ~1h
 15 by car\, ~EUR 30 of petrol. Hard-surface descents\, 90-110 m climbs. 
 Twenty reps is 1\,800 m of real ascent AND descent. One day there beats 
 ten stairwell sessions\, because sand is compliant and actually REDUCES 
 muscle damage relative to firm ground. Madeira is rock and stone steps.\
 n48 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,000-2
 \,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras heart rate 
 FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace off 
 knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n42 days to Ult
 ra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s1-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:Easy run 7 km
DESCRIPTION:Easy run 7 km (talk test) + 6-8 x 20 s strides after (relaxed
 \, full recovery\, not a workout)\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR unde
 r 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,0
 00-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras heart r
 ate FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace 
 off knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n39 days to
  Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s2-push@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:Push (upper)
DESCRIPTION:Push (upper) - after the easy run. Fresh\, not on legs you ju
 st destroyed.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~
 2\,000-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras hea
 rt rate FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. P
 ace off knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n39 day
 s to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s3-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260923
SUMMARY:◆ Legs ONLY\, no upper
DESCRIPTION:Legs ONLY\, no upper - heavy eccentric. Three quad lifts doin
 g three different jobs: HEAVY BILATERAL trap-bar deadlift 4 x 4-6 at 80-
 85% 1RM (~72-78 kg)\, LOADED UNILATERAL Bulgarian split squat 3 x 8/leg 
 with dumbbells\, and TEMPO ECCENTRIC step-downs 3 x 8-10/leg with 3-4 s 
 lowering. Then Nordics 3 x 5 and single-leg calf raises. Never to failur
 e. 48-72 h before the long day. On a -15% descent hip drop is 23.7 mm vs
  7.6 mm uphill (very large effect)\, so descending is a frontal-plane hi
 p problem and not only a quad problem - loaded Bulgarians carry that dem
 and\, which is why standalone side planks and cable abduction came out. 
 HYROX SLED TECHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% load (~100 kg)
 \, 60-90 s rest. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms hooked on t
 he posts\, 30-45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3-4 per secon
 d\, and never let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENTRIC\, so it 
 costs your descent block nothing - which is why it is the one Hyrox stat
 ion you can train now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of horizontal 
 force to break a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one rolling\, so l
 earning not to stop is worth more to you than to anyone heavier. About 8
  minutes.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,0
 00-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras heart r
 ate FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace 
 off knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n40 days to
  Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s4-vertical@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:▲ VERTICAL 75 min WITH INTERVALS
DESCRIPTION:VERTICAL 75 min WITH INTERVALS - stairwell. Warm up 10 min st
 eady\, then 4 x (5 min HARD up at 90-95% HRmax + 3 min EASY SkiErg or ro
 wer). Walk down between reps. Steady climbing for whatever time is left.
  This is the only hard session of your week and it does two jobs: uphill
  intervals for Madeira (the research wants 15-20% of training hard\, nea
 rly all of it on incline) and compromised running for Hyrox. The erg sta
 tions are deliberate - upper-body and aerobic\, so they add nothing to t
 he eccentric load your quads are already carrying.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Bu
 ild\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,000-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliab
 le as a guide: in mountain ultras heart rate FALLS ~34 bpm across the ra
 ce while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace off knee-extensor RPE - how you
 r quads feel - not the watch.\n38 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s5-pull@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:Pull (upper)
DESCRIPTION:Pull (upper) - after the vertical session. HYROX SEEDING\, al
 l substitutions not additions: (1) WARM UP ON THE SKIERG OR ROWER\, 5-8 
 min\, technique only - hinge and drive the first third of the pull\, tha
 t is where 80% of ski power comes from. Replaces your normal warm-up\, c
 osts nothing. (2) SWAP one row variation for a HEAVY FARMERS CARRY\, 4 x
  40-60 m. Same pulling pattern\, direct Hyrox transfer. (3) Finish with 
 DEAD HANGS\, 2-3 x max\, target 90 s by October. Grip takes 4-6 weeks to
  change and it is what limits the farmers carry. About 3 minutes total a
 dded to the session.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical week so 
 far\, ~2\,000-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ult
 ras heart rate FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to
  6.9. Pace off knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\
 n38 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s6-long@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260927
SUMMARY:▲ LONG DAY 2:55\, 1\,100 m vert\, full kit\, poles\,…
DESCRIPTION:LONG DAY 2:55\, 1\,100 m vert\, full kit\, poles\, 60 g/h DES
 CENT CUE: shorten the step\, 185-195 spm. Understriding cut strength los
 s to -8.8% vs -15.5% at preferred step length - roughly halved. Do NOT c
 oach foot strike: the more anterior the strike\, the LARGER the quad tor
 que loss. Let the terrain dictate it.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR 
 under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~
 2\,000-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras hea
 rt rate FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. P
 ace off knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n36 day
 s to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s7-descent@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
SUMMARY:▼ ZIG-ZAG AND WET-ROCK PRACTICE 45 min.…
DESCRIPTION:ZIG-ZAG AND WET-ROCK PRACTICE 45 min. Traversing at 60 deg to
  the fall line halves the gradient\, 28% -> 14%. Wet volcanic rock and w
 et wooden steps sit at friction 0.3-0.5 - barely enough to stand on a 28
 % slope\, let alone brake. In the wet\, zig-zagging and side-stepping ar
 e technique\, not cowardice.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical 
 week so far\, ~2\,000-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in moun
 tain ultras heart rate FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises fro
 m 4.3 to 6.9. Pace off knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the
  watch.\n42 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s8-descent@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260923
SUMMARY:▼ PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK
DESCRIPTION:PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK - 5 minutes\, 5.6 kg in the pac
 k\, walking DOWN stairs. Lift up\, walk down\, repeat for 5 min. ~110 m 
 of descent\, about 37 flights. One bout cuts strength loss 49%\, CK 47%\
 , soreness 66% a week later. Five minutes\, in your own building\, no tr
 avel.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,000-2
 \,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras heart rate 
 FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace off 
 knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n40 days to Ult
 ra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s9-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260921
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260922
SUMMARY:THRESHOLD (9 km)
DESCRIPTION:THRESHOLD - 5 x 5 min\, 90 s jog. Same effort as last week\, 
 one more rep. If the last rep is falling apart you went too hard on the 
 first.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Tal
 k test.\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,000-2\,300 m. HR is now unre
 liable as a guide: in mountain ultras heart rate FALLS ~34 bpm across th
 e race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace off knee-extensor RPE - how
  your quads feel - not the watch.\n41 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volume.
 \nCutback before the two biggest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM yo
 u need at least 2\,250 kcal before exercise is counted - peak-week days 
 run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under-fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most likel
 y route to a stress fracture\, and your body mass must not trend down.\n
 35 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
