BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w14-s4-vertical@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261008
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:▲ VERTICAL 80 min WITH INTERVALS
DESCRIPTION:VERTICAL 80 min WITH INTERVALS - stairwell. Warm up 10 min st
 eady\, then 5 x (5 min HARD up at 90-95% HRmax + 3 min EASY SkiErg or ro
 wer). Walk down between reps. Steady climbing for whatever time is left.
  This is the only hard session of your week and it does two jobs: uphill
  intervals for Madeira (the research wants 15-20% of training hard\, nea
 rly all of it on incline) and compromised running for Hyrox. The erg sta
 tions are deliberate - upper-body and aerobic\, so they add nothing to t
 he eccentric load your quads are already carrying.\n\nWeek 14 of 17 - Pe
 ak\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #2 - POSBANK AGAIN\, not the Ardennes. Roughly EUR 3
 0 of petrol against EUR 200\, and twenty reps of a 90-110 m climb is 1\,
 800 m of ascent AND hard-surface descent - close to the whole race. Sust
 ained descending on firm ground is the one thing stairs cannot replicate
 \, and it is what decides your day. POLES: bought 18-20 Sep\, so you hav
 e had three weeks on them by now. Use them the whole session. They cut R
 PE 14-18% and measurably reduce muscle damage over a climb-and-descent d
 ay - but an inexperienced pole user in a field study actually got SLOWER
 \, so the practice is the point. KIT-CHECK HABIT STARTS HERE: every food
  item must be labelled with its calorie count\, and all disposable packa
 ging must carry your bib number. Tape a strip on your gel flask reading 
 contents and total kcal (e.g. '4x Upfront Gel PRO - 640 kcal'). Do it fr
 om this session on\, not at registration.\n24 days to Ultra X Madeira 25
 K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
