DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:Pull (upper)
DESCRIPTION:Pull (upper) - after the vertical session. HYROX SEEDING\, al
 l substitutions not additions: (1) WARM UP ON THE SKIERG OR ROWER\, 5-8 
 min\, technique only - hinge and drive the first third of the pull\, tha
 t is where 80% of ski power comes from. Replaces your normal warm-up\, c
 osts nothing. (2) SWAP one row variation for a HEAVY FARMERS CARRY\, 4 x
  40-60 m. Same pulling pattern\, direct Hyrox transfer. (3) Finish with 
 DEAD HANGS\, 2-3 x max\, target 90 s by October. Grip takes 4-6 weeks to
  change and it is what limits the farmers carry. About 3 minutes total a
 dded to the session.\n\nWeek 14 of 17 - Peak\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #2 - POSBA
 NK AGAIN\, not the Ardennes. Roughly EUR 30 of petrol against EUR 200\, 
 and twenty reps of a 90-110 m climb is 1\,800 m of ascent AND hard-surfa
 ce descent - close to the whole race. Sustained descending on firm groun
 d is the one thing stairs cannot replicate\, and it is what decides your
  day. POLES: bought 18-20 Sep\, so you have had three weeks on them by n
 ow. Use them the whole session. They cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduc
 e muscle damage over a climb-and-descent day - but an inexperienced pole
  user in a field study actually got SLOWER\, so the practice is the poin
 t. KIT-CHECK HABIT STARTS HERE: every food item must be labelled with it
 s calorie count\, and all disposable packaging must carry your bib numbe
 r. Tape a strip on your gel flask reading contents and total kcal (e.g. 
 '4x Upfront Gel PRO - 640 kcal'). Do it from this session on\, not at re
 gistration.\n24 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
