DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261005
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261006
SUMMARY:THRESHOLD (9 km)
DESCRIPTION:THRESHOLD - 5 x 5 min comfortably hard\, 90 s jog. NOT VO2max
 : Thursday's stairs are already a VO2max session (5 x 5 min at 90-95% HR
 max) and two of those in one week on 30 km of running is how people get 
 hurt in October. Flat threshold and stair VO2max cover different things 
 - that is the point.\n\nWeek 14 of 17 - Peak\nKeep HR under 158. Walk th
 e climbs. Talk test.\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #2 - POSBANK AGAIN\, not the Arden
 nes. Roughly EUR 30 of petrol against EUR 200\, and twenty reps of a 90-
 110 m climb is 1\,800 m of ascent AND hard-surface descent - close to th
 e whole race. Sustained descending on firm ground is the one thing stair
 s cannot replicate\, and it is what decides your day. POLES: bought 18-2
 0 Sep\, so you have had three weeks on them by now. Use them the whole s
 ession. They cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduce muscle damage over a c
 limb-and-descent day - but an inexperienced pole user in a field study a
 ctually got SLOWER\, so the practice is the point. KIT-CHECK HABIT START
 S HERE: every food item must be labelled with its calorie count\, and al
 l disposable packaging must carry your bib number. Tape a strip on your 
 gel flask reading contents and total kcal (e.g. '4x Upfront Gel PRO - 64
 0 kcal'). Do it from this session on\, not at registration.\n27 days to 
 Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
