BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w15-s3-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:◆ Legs ONLY\, no upper
DESCRIPTION:Legs ONLY\, no upper - heavy eccentric. Three quad lifts doin
 g three different jobs: HEAVY BILATERAL trap-bar deadlift 4 x 4-6 at 80-
 85% 1RM (~72-78 kg)\, LOADED UNILATERAL Bulgarian split squat 3 x 8/leg 
 with dumbbells\, and TEMPO ECCENTRIC step-downs 3 x 8-10/leg with 3-4 s 
 lowering. Then Nordics 3 x 5 and single-leg calf raises. Never to failur
 e. 48-72 h before the long day. On a -15% descent hip drop is 23.7 mm vs
  7.6 mm uphill (very large effect)\, so descending is a frontal-plane hi
 p problem and not only a quad problem - loaded Bulgarians carry that dem
 and\, which is why standalone side planks and cable abduction came out. 
 HYROX SLED TECHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% load (~100 kg)
 \, 60-90 s rest. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms hooked on t
 he posts\, 30-45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3-4 per secon
 d\, and never let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENTRIC\, so it 
 costs your descent block nothing - which is why it is the one Hyrox stat
 ion you can train now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of horizontal 
 force to break a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one rolling\, so l
 earning not to stop is worth more to you than to anyone heavier. About 8
  minutes.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days o
 ut. This is the overload the taper is built on\; the evidence favours pe
 aking 14-15 days out\, not five weeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,800 m: ro
 ughly 60-70% of race duration but 80-90% of race vertical. Vertical spec
 ificity is the lever\, not duration.\n19 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
