DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:▲ PEAK LONG DAY 3:45-4:00\, 1\,600-1\,800 m vert.…
DESCRIPTION:PEAK LONG DAY 3:45-4:00\, 1\,600-1\,800 m vert. Race kit\, po
 les\, race fuelling\, race shoes. Alternate 20-25 min climbing with 15-2
 0 min flat to rehearse the sawtooth. DESCENT CUE: shorten the step\, 185
 -195 spm. Understriding cut strength loss to -8.8% vs -15.5% at preferre
 d step length - roughly halved. Do NOT coach foot strike: the more anter
 ior the strike\, the LARGER the quad torque loss. Let the terrain dictat
 e it.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk 
 test.\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days out. This is the overload the
  taper is built on\; the evidence favours peaking 14-15 days out\, not f
 ive weeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,800 m: roughly 60-70% of race duratio
 n but 80-90% of race vertical. Vertical specificity is the lever\, not d
 uration.\n15 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w15-s7-descent@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:▼ PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK
DESCRIPTION:PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK - 5 minutes\, 5.6 kg in the pac
 k\, walking DOWN stairs. Lift up\, walk down\, repeat for 5 min. ~110 m 
 of descent\, about 37 flights. One bout cuts strength loss 49%\, CK 47%\
 , soreness 66% a week later. Five minutes\, in your own building\, no tr
 avel.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days out. 
 This is the overload the taper is built on\; the evidence favours peakin
 g 14-15 days out\, not five weeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,800 m: roughl
 y 60-70% of race duration but 80-90% of race vertical. Vertical specific
 ity is the lever\, not duration.\n19 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
