 3:45-4:00 with 1\,600-1\,800 m of vert\, and that session matters more t
 han any interval you could run on a Monday. Protect it.\n\nWeek 15 of 17
  - Peak\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nPEAK WEEKEND - 
 Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days out. This is the overload the taper is built on\; t
 he evidence favours peaking 14-15 days out\, not five weeks. 3:45-4:00 a
 nd 1\,600-1\,800 m: roughly 60-70% of race duration but 80-90% of race v
 ertical. Vertical specificity is the lever\, not duration.\n20 days to U
 ltra X Madeira 25K.
