END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w17-s0-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Easy shakeout 5 km
DESCRIPTION:Easy shakeout 5 km\n\nWeek 17 of 17 - Race\nKeep HR under 158
 . Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nRACE WEEK. Sunday 1 Nov\, Calhau de Sao J
 orge to Machico. THE START IS 11:00\, NOT DAWN - sunset is 18:17 and civ
 il twilight ends 18:41. A 6:30 finish is daylight\; 7:00 is dusk\; 7:30 
 is DARK on exposed cliff paths. YOUR HEADTORCH IS SAFETY KIT\, NOT A FOR
 MALITY - carry it charged. The late start also gives you an unhurried fu
 elling morning: eat properly\, this is an advantage. CHECKPOINTS ARE WAT
 ER ONLY - the 'water and snacks' line is wrong. Carry 420-490 g of carbo
 hydrate yourself (~13 gels plus mix) across three ~2h10 legs\, roughly 2
 .6 kg of vest. Only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart. KIT: 1.5 L hydration 
 capacity\, taped-seam hooded waterproof\, emergency blanket\, 800 kcal r
 eserve\, phone with GPX\, spare warm layer\, and a BEAKER of at least 15
  cl - bottles and flasks are explicitly not accepted. Checks are enforce
 d. CALIBRATION from the 2025 field (n=34): winner 3:02:21\, median 5:24:
 37 (13.0 min/km)\, last finisher 8:03:43\, cut-off 11.5 h. Your target i
 s 6:15-6:45. The 25K is the final 25 km of the 50K route - the organiser
  gave the SHORT race the STEEPEST ground\, 80 m/km against 63.5 for the 
 50K. PACING - the single strongest result in the literature (n=23\,207):
  in 91% of races\, slower finishers overspent in the FIRST segment\; aft
 er the opening everyone paces the rest alike. The damage is done at the 
 start. Hike every gradient above 15% from the gun. HR: race average 138-
 150\, climb ceiling 155\, descents 120-140. Above 160 for two minutes on
  a climb\, walk. Your 17 km run averaged 163 - you cannot hold that for 
 six hours. THE DESCENT IS THE RACE. Racing the first steep descent saves
  ~10 minutes and costs 17-46 minutes later: 3:1 to 5:1 against\, before 
 you count the fall risk. And it will never feel hard - VO2 on descents i
 s only 79% of threshold versus 100% uphill\, so your breathing will tell
  you nothing. That is the trap. Short steps\, 185-195 spm\, gaze 4-5 m a
 head on the second upcoming foothold\, walk the stone staircases\, zig-z
 ag the wet sections. IN-RACE DIAGNOSTIC: compare climb rate per heartbea
 t on the second climb against the first. More than 5% worse means you ov
 ercooked the descent - concede ten minutes immediately and save the day.
  FUEL: 60-75 g/h at 2:1 glucose:fructose\, drink to thirst\, skip the sa
 lt capsules (no evidence they prevent hyponatraemia or cramp). Carb load
  8-10 g/kg for 36-48 h = 450-560 g. Caffeine ~100 mg at 3 h and 75-100 m
 g at 4.5 h\, 150-200 mg total - do not scale from 70 kg examples. WEATHE
 R: use Santana on the north coast\, not Funchal - 18 C max\, 110 mm of r
 ain across ~40% of days. Wet basalt and hypothermia are the risks here\,
  not heat. Bib pickup Fri 30 Oct or Sat 31 Oct\, 18:00-20:00\, Machico F
 orum. No crew\, no pacers\, no drop bags.\n6 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K
 .
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w17-s1-strides@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T215856Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261029
SUMMARY:Easy 3-4 km + 4 x 90 s at race-climb effort
DESCRIPTION:Easy 3-4 km + 4 x 90 s at race-climb effort. Do not skip this
 .\n\nWeek 17 of 17 - Race\nRACE WEEK. Sunday 1 Nov\, Calhau de Sao Jorge
  to Machico. THE START IS 11:00\, NOT DAWN - sunset is 18:17 and civil t
 wilight ends 18:41. A 6:30 finish is daylight\; 7:00 is dusk\; 7:30 is D
 ARK on exposed cliff paths. YOUR HEADTORCH IS SAFETY KIT\, NOT A FORMALI
 TY - carry it charged. The late start also gives you an unhurried fuelli
 ng morning: eat properly\, this is an advantage. CHECKPOINTS ARE WATER O
 NLY - the 'water and snacks' line is wrong. Carry 420-490 g of carbohydr
 ate yourself (~13 gels plus mix) across three ~2h10 legs\, roughly 2.6 k
 g of vest. Only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart. KIT: 1.5 L hydration capa
 city\, taped-seam hooded waterproof\, emergency blanket\, 800 kcal reser
 ve\, phone with GPX\, spare warm layer\, and a BEAKER of at least 15 cl 
 - bottles and flasks are explicitly not accepted. Checks are enforced. C
 ALIBRATION from the 2025 field (n=34): winner 3:02:21\, median 5:24:37 (
 13.0 min/km)\, last finisher 8:03:43\, cut-off 11.5 h. Your target is 6:
 15-6:45. The 25K is the final 25 km of the 50K route - the organiser gav
 e the SHORT race the STEEPEST ground\, 80 m/km against 63.5 for the 50K.
  PACING - the single strongest result in the literature (n=23\,207): in 
 91% of races\, slower finishers overspent in the FIRST segment\; after t
 he opening everyone paces the rest alike. The damage is done at the star
 t. Hike every gradient above 15% from the gun. HR: race average 138-150\
 , climb ceiling 155\, descents 120-140. Above 160 for two minutes on a c
 limb\, walk. Your 17 km run averaged 163 - you cannot hold that for six 
 hours. THE DESCENT IS THE RACE. Racing the first steep descent saves ~10
  minutes and costs 17-46 minutes later: 3:1 to 5:1 against\, before you 
 count the fall risk. And it will never feel hard - VO2 on descents is on
 ly 79% of threshold versus 100% uphill\, so your breathing will tell you
  nothing. That is the trap. Short steps\, 185-195 spm\, gaze 4-5 m ahead
  on the second upcoming foothold\, walk the stone staircases\, zig-zag t
 he wet sections. IN-RACE DIAGNOSTIC: compare climb rate per heartbeat on
  the second climb against the first. More than 5% worse means you overco
 oked the descent - concede ten minutes immediately and save the day. FUE
 L: 60-75 g/h at 2:1 glucose:fructose\, drink to thirst\, skip the salt c
 apsules (no evidence they prevent hyponatraemia or cramp). Carb load 8-1
 0 g/kg for 36-48 h = 450-560 g. Caffeine ~100 mg at 3 h and 75-100 mg at
  4.5 h\, 150-200 mg total - do not scale from 70 kg examples. WEATHER: u
 se Santana on the north coast\, not Funchal - 18 C max\, 110 mm of rain 
 across ~40% of days. Wet basalt and hypothermia are the risks here\, not
  heat. Bib pickup Fri 30 Oct or Sat 31 Oct\, 18:00-20:00\, Machico Forum
 . No crew\, no pacers\, no drop bags.\n4 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
